^{:go/pos {:doc [179 1] :lparen [188 7] :rparen [191 1] :tok-pos [188 1]}} (go/const "The handles' reference counts (queue 262; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 262\"): a proxy's ob_refcnt counts\nthe references C holds, Python's own references being Go's. A proxy is made with count 0 (a borrowed reference: an\nargument, a container's item); a new reference C receives raises it (newRef), Py_DecRef lowers it. A proxy whose\ncount is 0 is released when the outermost C entry ends (capiLeave: a ctypes foreign call, an extension module's\nfunction, its PyInit), after the result was taken: its map entries dropped (the object is Go's again alone) and its\nmemory freed. A borrowed reference is so valid until the Python code that called C runs again, as CPython's while\nits owner holds it. Types and the singletons are immortal (never released): their count is CPython's\n_Py_IMMORTAL_INITIAL_REFCNT, which Include/refcount.h's inline Py_INCREF leaves alone (>= it) and Py_DECREF too\n(_Py_IsImmortal: >= _Py_IMMORTAL_MINIMUM_REFCNT).\n"
